            "review_title": "Review at Phan Thiet Quan",
            "review_text": "Mariann E\nBudapest, Hungary40 contributions\n0\nRare and strange, but delicious dishes\nFeb 2014 • Couples\nWe visited Phan Thiết Quán once, but I wish to go back there cause I couldn’t try everything.\nMost of the dishes are special ones that are not sold at any other restaurant in Vietnam, such as fried rice with seafood, spanner crab, blood shell with wasabi, prawn with wasabi.\nThey cook all these in a new way, it was surprising and delicious. This was the first place where I ate really tasty squid. And the ones I didn’t dare to try yet are iguana made in different ways, and king spike snail. And even the rare ones are quite cheap compare to other places.\n\nIf you are fed up with regular food, go to Phan Thiết Quán!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 15, 2014",
